--- key exec --help
CMD: /evidence/oh-my-cpa key exec --help
EXIT: 0
STDOUT:
Usage: oh-my-cpa key exec --runtime <claude|codex|opencode> [--repo <repo>] [--base-url <url>] [--home <dir>] -- <command> [args...]

Opens the repository's envelope in memory and runs <command> with only the
variables that runtime needs. The plaintext is never written to disk, never
printed and never put in this process's command line. The child inherits
stdin, stdout, stderr and the rest of the environment.

claude    sets ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN; removes
          ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for the child because it may take precedence
codex     requires <command> to be codex itself; inserts -c provider
          overrides and passes the key through OMC_REPO_KEY (Codex is not
          known to select a provider from the environment alone)
opencode  sets OPENCODE_CONFIG_CONTENT to the user's configuration merged
          with provider.oh-my-cpa; the key is in that variable only

--repo defaults to the repository of the current directory (its git origin,
or the directory name when there is no remote).

Everything after -- is the command and its arguments, passed through
unchanged: this command runs no shell and expands nothing.

The command's exit code becomes this command's exit code once the command
has started.
STDERR:
ASSERT C-01 exec-help exit=0 PASS
ASSERT C-01 top-help lists exec PASS
--- key install --help
CMD: /evidence/oh-my-cpa key install --help
EXIT: 0
STDOUT:
Usage: oh-my-cpa key install --runtime <claude|codex|opencode> [--repo <repo>] [--base-url <url>] [--config <path>] [--replace] [--home <dir>]

Writes the repository key into the runtime's own configuration file. This is
the only command that leaves the plaintext key on disk, and it says so on
stderr before it writes. The previous file is copied into $OMC_HOME/backups/
first when it exists.

  claude    ~/.claude/settings.json, env.ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL and
            env.ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (or $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/settings.json)
  codex     $CODEX_HOME/config.toml or ~/.codex/config.toml, a managed
            [model_providers.oh-my-cpa] table plus model_provider
  opencode  ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json, provider.oh-my-cpa.options
            (or $OPENCODE_CONFIG)

Only the user-level file of each runtime is written: a project-level
.claude/settings.json belongs to a repository and would end up committed with
the key in it.

One installed slot per runtime per machine. Installing another repository
replaces the slot only with --replace (or after purging the other repository);
without it the install stops with config_owned_by_another_repo. The previous
values survive only in the backup. --replace is also required when the slot
holds a value this tool did not write.

--repo defaults to the repository of the current directory. --config names
the configuration file instead of the runtime's default.
